# Accepted residual CVEs. Every entry documents why it is accepted and when to
# remove it. The Trivy gate in the release flow must pass with ONLY these
# suppressions -- a new finding means a new decision, not a new entry by reflex.
#
# SCOPE: this file is the complete app-image allowlist. The release gate builds
# the tts and render allowlists from reviewed static per-image membership before
# adding their image-specific files; it explicitly removes the app/tts-only
# libsndfile entry from the render allowlist.
# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck all retained entries: 2026-10-10.

# -- Debian trixie base (python:*-slim): no fixed package released yet.
# Remove each when `apt-get upgrade` in a rebuild clears it from the scan.

# perl / perl-base / libperl5.40 / perl-modules-5.40 (CRITICAL x3, HIGH x4):
# interpreter ships in the slim base; nothing in Audicle invokes perl.
# Statuses: CVE-2026-8376, CVE-2026-48962, CVE-2026-13221 and CVE-2026-57432
# are "affected"; the other three are "fix_deferred". All seven are equally
# not-yet-fixed in trixie.
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-9538
# regex engine silently-incorrect-match (CRITICAL) and S_measure_struct integer
# overflow (HIGH), added 0.48.2:
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-57432

# curl / libcurl4t64 / libcurl3t64-gnutls (HIGH x3):
# system curl ships in base; backend Python httpx does not use system libcurl.
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-8927

# ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin) (HIGH x1):
# terminal handling in base; Audicle runs headless in a container.
CVE-2025-69720

# gzip (HIGH x1): compression utility in base; not invoked by application code.
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1 (HIGH x1): POSIX ACL library in base; no ACL operations in Audicle.
CVE-2026-54369

# libsndfile1 (HIGH x1): CVE-2026-37555 is an integer overflow in the IMA
# ADPCM WAV parser. Reference uploads accepted directly by Python's wave module
# are PCM; every other reference format and every chime upload is decoded by
# ffmpeg and stored as PCM before soundfile reads it. Bundled TTS chunks are also
# PCM. Audio from an explicitly configured remote TTS provider is decoded by the
# controlled ffmpeg subprocess to PCM16 before storage, ASR, caching, duration
# inspection, or soundfile, so provider bytes cannot reach the vulnerable IMA
# ADPCM parser. No Debian fix is available.
# Present in app and tts images; included here so the app scan (shared-only) passes.
CVE-2026-37555

# perl Storable (perl-base in app/render; libperl5.40, perl, perl-base,
# perl-modules-5.40 in tts) (CRITICAL x1, "affected"): signed integer overflow
# in Storable before 3.41 (CVE-2026-57433). Perl rides in the Debian base;
# no application code invokes perl or deserializes Storable data. No Debian
# fix released. Added 0.48.3. Remove when trixie ships a patched perl.
CVE-2026-57433

# CVE-2026-8458 (curl/libcurl, HIGH): unauthorized connection reuse. No fixed
# package exists in Debian trixie as of 2026-08-10 (trivy status: affected,
# empty fixed-version). Present in all three images, which is why it lives in
# the shared file: each installs curl solely for the localhost container
# healthcheck; article fetching uses httpx, never libcurl. Re-check each
# release and drop this entry when deb13u ships a fixed curl.
CVE-2026-8458

# CVE-2026-58050 (libssh2-1t64, HIGH): the publickey-subsystem attribute-count
# multiplication can overflow only on 32-bit platforms; the release app and GPU
# wrapper images are amd64. libssh2 arrives through healthcheck curl, which makes
# only localhost HTTP requests. The wrapper Dockerfile also installs git for its
# dependency-install layer and currently retains it in the GPU runtime, but the
# lock resolves dependencies from PyPI, runtime code never invokes git, no SSH
# client is installed, and neither git+HTTPS nor curl HTTP calls libssh2's
# publickey-list API. No fixed trixie package is available. Remove this entry
# when deb13u ships a fixed libssh2.
CVE-2026-58050

# CVE-2026-11822 / CVE-2026-11824 (libsqlite3-0, HIGH x2): memory corruption in
# the FTS5 full-text extension, reachable only by opening a crafted database
# and running an FTS5 MATCH query against it. No fixed package in Debian trixie
# as of 2026-09-02 (trivy status: affected, empty fixed-version); the fix is
# upstream SQLite 3.53.2 and the base ships 3.46.1-7+deb13u1. Present in all
# three images because Python's sqlite3 links the system library. Audicle
# creates no FTS5 tables and issues no MATCH queries, and it only ever opens
# the database it owns in its own volume, never an operator- or user-supplied
# file. Re-check each release and drop these when deb13u ships a fixed sqlite3.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10.
# CVE-2026-16742 affects systemd-homed record verification. None of the images
# runs systemd-homed. The four util-linux findings affect privileged mount and
# nsenter operations; the services run as nonroot with no capabilities and do
# not invoke those tools. Debian 13 has no fixed package versions for these IDs.
CVE-2026-16742
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410
